{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/436851-too-much-homebrew","id":436851,"title":"Too much Homebrew?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-11T02:25:35-07:00","id":436851,"title":"Too much Homebrew?","content":"When my group played Scion, we found that once you hit demigod, the system just stopped working quite how it seemed to in Scion. They were also disappointed that even in Demi-God the powers were too precise to give the same epic feeling, add in that many of the concepts for some characters seemed to fall flat with how clinical the system was. A god of music was just really good at music and a goddess of sorrow just had to be very precise how they used epic manipulation.<br /> <br /> So we made house Rules, and then we sorta shopped around for rules in other games that fit, because we were really devoted to the world, but felt the rules left much to be desired.<br /> <br /> I found an RPG called Part Time Gods, whose rules were well conceived if the application a little clunky, and we sorta...combined the 2?<br /> <br /> In Part Time Gods, You can be a god of nearly anything which sorta suits myths where the Patron God of specific rivers were common. But what was interesting was instead of building up 1 specific ability for each, an impossible task, they built on ways you use powers.<br /> <br /> So a God of Sorrow could concentrate on Minion to summon ghosts who died from grief, or Puppetry to influence other people who are suffering from sorrow and even take control. All the while the Goddess of Music can assault the ears of those around her with Ruin (every bit as good as the god of Fire with Ruin) or she could use Aegis to protect musicians.While if they took Shaping, the God of Sorrow could make himself look like a grieving neighbors recently dead daughter, while the Goddess of music could make an opera singer warble like a 1940s crooner or make the most off tune child learning the piano into a maestro.<br /> <br /> Of course we mixed them, and there were specific pantheon things as well, a separate skill building things unique to them also we made all of the others things you could build upon as well so there were levels than just how good you were with dice. We replaced the knacks with other less focused powers and got rid of a few Attributes (appearance and Perception) realized that made Physical too lopsided so added Wisdom and Will in their place. Got rid of Willpower and added some effects to legend, got rid of the idea of increasing past 6 in any attribute and only 2 (or 3 with a flaw also things we added) epics per tier. Legend was severely changed, while fatebound remained mostly intact.<br /> <br /> Also, you can be a God of multiple things but roleplay is required and sometimes it is by accident. One of her followers finds out that the Goddess of Music used to be a waitress, she can easily start growing as the Patron Goddess of Waiters as well (which also makes sense why some Gods in myth are bizarrely eclectic) and weirdly enough Patron Goddess of Waiters isn't the worst gig.<br /> <br /> My point being, at this point is it even Scion? Is there a point where you aren't just making homebrew rules and you just made a jumbled mishmash? Should I layer back in future games, and just play the original Scion? Especially since there are so many rule changes. It feels eerily wrong to mess with a game that much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5197-kadakithis","name":"kadakithis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T08:58:07-07:00","id":437085,"title":"","content":"If someone from another Scion group came in, how much explaining would you have to do to get them up and playing? If it's more than a short conversation (or document), then you are probably playing something different. Something you created based on Scion's mechanics, yes, but more on Scion's themes. <br /> <br /> Every Scion game I have run or been in has fallen apart at Demigod. The game just became uninteresting from the point of view of how the mechanics affected the story for many of the reasons you have stated and a lot of others that have been discussed at length in other posts. I know people have played Scion to the point of God and I have discussed with them how they did so. My impression is that, largely, a lot of House Rules are brought into play and/or the rules fall away and the game becomes a much more freeform interaction. <br /> <br /> I've backed away from Scion, until I can see what the new rules are like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T11:00:11-07:00","id":437236,"title":"","content":"I had to end a game of Scion because when we reached Demigod, I was basically rewriting the entire game to allow things to function. The original system just doesn't <i>work</i> past Legend 4. It doesn't even really work <i>well</i> <b>at</b> Legend 4.<br /> <br /> You may not be playing Scion, but if you're having fun, carry on. Scion's not really a playable game so much as a cool idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T17:14:19-07:00","id":437731,"title":"","content":"I think Ajax hit it on the head when he said that if you cannot explain the difference easily, then it is not a Scion game anymore but just a game based on Scion themes. Themes which, I will reaily admit, are fan-freaking-tastic. However, the rules breakdown very quickly. I know that the changes I made were changing Epic Attributes into using the Mega-Attribute system. I also put up Knack Trees and the Knacks all had Legend minimums and tried my absolute damndest to retain the Scion rules. Unfortunately, the game could not sustain itself for too long since I felt that I was bailing water out of the leak in my canoe with a teaspoon.<br /> Here's to hoping 2nd Edition kicks ass. We all love the game. The passion displayed by the players of it is phenomenal. We just need rules that work that we do not have to homebrew to keep it sustainable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T17:44:42-07:00","id":437796,"title":"","content":"For me the &quot;moment&quot; was when I had to cancel a game so I could <i>write enough powers </i>for my players to spend experience. I realized I was writing a whole new book and I just didn't have time for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T18:29:18-07:00","id":437833,"title":"","content":"I was one of those players, though I was definitely trying NOT to have Telgar write more powers for my own character as I was running a different Scion game at the same time and going through the same thing in that game as well. I could both sympathize and empathize with what he was going through<br /> <br /> It was a meltdown situation rules-wise, leaving a lot of radioactive rubble where Scion RAW used to be. My group just shifted over to playing a nice simple limited plot Vampire game to decompress, wait for M20 to come out, play that, THEN hopefully Scion:God 2d Ed will be out and we can peep out of our underground bunker and see what the renewed world above-ground looks like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T14:01:11-07:00","id":440448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kadakithis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/436851-too-much-homebrew#post436851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point being, at this point is it even Scion? Is there a point where you aren't just making homebrew rules and you just made a jumbled mishmash? Should I layer back in future games, and just play the original Scion? Especially since there are so many rule changes. It feels eerily wrong to mess with a game that much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Original Scion has so many issues mechanically that I would not suggest going with it. There are some really great house rules floating around, such as Gotham By Night or Scion 2.0, but you are right in the sense that those houserules are so far removed from the core game as to effectively no longer be playing Scion anymore.<br /> <br /> But if everyone is having fun, who cares if you are playing a Frankenstein system?<br /> Things only get awkward when you are trying to introduce a new player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T16:48:26-07:00","id":440633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/436851-too-much-homebrew?p=440448#post440448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Things only get awkward when you are trying to introduce a new player.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is not an inconsequential concern. Not just a new player, but joining or creating a new group. RAW need to be strong enough to hold a game together. When you see what people did to make Scion work for them... (vide Gotham By Night), it gets so idiosyncratic that it's very hard to figure out what is even going on if you aren't already an initiate of that system. If the best way to approach the rules of your Scion game is that the player needs to have been there the whole time or the person has to come to the table with no preconceived notions about the mechanics (like say, from reading the books), then you have a portability issues. And portability issues result in a breakdown of the community of people playing the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T20:36:25-07:00","id":440826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/436851-too-much-homebrew?p=440633#post440633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is not an inconsequential concern. Not just a new player, but joining or creating a new group. RAW need to be strong enough to hold a game together. When you see what people did to make Scion work for them... (vide Gotham By Night), it gets so idiosyncratic that it's very hard to figure out what is even going on if you aren't already an initiate of that system. If the best way to approach the rules of your Scion game is that the player needs to have been there the whole time or the person has to come to the table with no preconceived notions about the mechanics (like say, from reading the books), then you have a portability issues. And portability issues result in a breakdown of the community of people playing the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the most part I agree. Everyone should always have the expectation that they will be dealing with house rules when they join a new gaming group. Who has not experienced going from one gaming group with fun house rules to another gaming group with irritating house rules? Even well known gaming systems like D&amp;D will be moderately to heavily house ruled from one gaming table to the next, unless you are primarily playing at sanctioned events.<br /> <br /> But Scion absolutely takes a step off the deep end because of the sheer quantity of house rules that are necessary to play the game beyond Legend 4. This contributes significantly to the portability issues you reference, and may create a very unpleasant learning curve anytime you want to play at someone else's table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T09:03:39-07:00","id":441381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/436851-too-much-homebrew?p=440826#post440826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the most part I agree. Everyone should always have the expectation that they will be dealing with house rules when they join a new gaming group. Who has not experienced going from one gaming group with fun house rules to another gaming group with irritating house rules? Even well known gaming systems like D&amp;D will be moderately to heavily house ruled from one gaming table to the next, unless you are primarily playing at sanctioned events.<br /> <br /> But Scion absolutely takes a step off the deep end because of the sheer quantity of house rules that are necessary to play the game beyond Legend 4. This contributes significantly to the portability issues you reference, and may create a very unpleasant learning curve anytime you want to play at someone else's table.</div> </div> </div> </div>And, as in my case and as I have seen in other games, a cost-benefit analysis for the game, particularly the Storyteller, about how much work they are willing to do to keep the game going. Which, also in the same cases, causes good games with good stories to just <i><b>end</b></i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}